    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-129405",
      "knowledge_point_id": "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\n- The limit evaluates to $2$ along the path $y=0$\n- The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{3}$ along the path $y=x$\n- The limit does not exist",
      "worked_solution": "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{2({0}^{2})-{0}^{2}}{{0}^{2}+2({0}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0}{0+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{0}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2({0}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is also true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{3\\cancel{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
